                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2584670c-3ea7-44ee-8927-b53b0e5074bf",
                        "source_entry_id": "52847385-4bcc-32a5-b78d-2f07d95e3f97",
                        "source_sense_id": "ac5853e8-2bde-38e0-a9ad-3c684ef6494d",
                        "target_lang_word": "starry",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "starry",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d0172527-70b1-34eb-8141-66549bc7f65c",
                                        "entry_id": "21b4e020-3134-3874-acb6-c4fda2c989c5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having stars visible."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f40ceac-c1a9-4f31-818d-cbf51f45ed4c",
                                                "sense_id": "d0172527-70b1-34eb-8141-66549bc7f65c",
                                                "text": "starry night"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "13411db1-42ed-449d-8a20-402c0fb6f418",
                                                "sense_id": "d0172527-70b1-34eb-8141-66549bc7f65c",
                                                "text": "Alyssa stared out of her window at the starry night sky."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "196dd66d-1131-3ee6-b389-642873d95817",
                                        "entry_id": "21b4e020-3134-3874-acb6-c4fda2c989c5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Resembling or shaped like a star."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3fa6bb7e-61ec-4e79-a1f8-300396801965",
                                                "sense_id": "196dd66d-1131-3ee6-b389-642873d95817",
                                                "text": "I shrank from the starry waters as they rose to my lip, but a power stronger than my will compelled me to their taste."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0bcf63b-61ca-4007-abfb-591d1eadad67",
                                                "sense_id": "196dd66d-1131-3ee6-b389-642873d95817",
                                                "text": "An old shrub long grown in gardens for its irregular yellow flowers of peculiar starry shape, coming from October to December."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e2183461-0890-3ce4-83b2-071946ecb032",
                                        "entry_id": "21b4e020-3134-3874-acb6-c4fda2c989c5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Full of stars or celebrities."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2953cbf-d265-4163-9454-47f997dac64f",
                                                "sense_id": "e2183461-0890-3ce4-83b2-071946ecb032",
                                                "text": "Despite a starry cast, the film performed poorly at the box office."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20f78fc4-bf1b-4e12-a89b-352d8f86ceda",
                                                "sense_id": "e2183461-0890-3ce4-83b2-071946ecb032",
                                                "text": "A starry 20th-anniversary revival of “Topdog/Underdog,” her Pulitzer Prize-winning fable about two brothers, three-card monte and one troubling inheritance, is in previews on Broadway."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77ea0576-41dd-42a5-9ec5-a441c23a574a",
                                                "sense_id": "e2183461-0890-3ce4-83b2-071946ecb032",
                                                "text": "After a bit of digging, we discovered she follows a stringent workout and nutrition regime, masterminded by Patrick Murphy — a celeb PT with a super-starry roster, including Zac Efron, Keanu Reeves and Ruby Rose — with a focus on overall health rather than aesthetics."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f207af8a-0325-43b2-a831-f4d667433d32",
                        "source_entry_id": "52847385-4bcc-32a5-b78d-2f07d95e3f97",
                        "source_sense_id": "ac5853e8-2bde-38e0-a9ad-3c684ef6494d",
                        "target_lang_word": "starlit",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "starlit",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bb2a8294-bcc9-37b1-9baf-92c84ed05fe2",
                                        "entry_id": "e6933efc-847f-30a7-8856-a0ec3757509c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Illuminated by starlight."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a1763a9-d104-4511-8476-52a949c08b34",
                                                "sense_id": "bb2a8294-bcc9-37b1-9baf-92c84ed05fe2",
                                                "text": "BEHIND him lay the gray Azores,/ Behind the Gates of Hercules; / Before him not the ghost of shores, / Before him only shoreless seas. // The good mate said: “Now must we pray, / For lo! the very stars are gone. / Brave Admiral, speak, what shall I say?” / “Why, say, ‘Sail on! sail on! and on!’”\n“My men grow mutinous day by day; / My men grow ghastly wan and weak.” / The stout mate thought of home; a spray / Of salt wave washed his swarthy cheek. // “What shall I say, brave Admiral, say, / If we sight naught but seas at dawn?” / “Why, you shall say at break of day, / ‘Sail on! sail on! sail on! and on!’”\nThey sailed and sailed, as winds might blow, / Until at last the blanched mate said: / “Why, now not even God would know / Should I and all my men fall dead. // These very winds forget their way, / For God from these dread seas is gone. / Now speak, brave Admiral, speak and say”— / He said: “Sail on! sail on! and on!”\nThey sailed. They sailed. Then spake the mate: / “This mad sea shows his teeth to-night. / He curls his lip, he lies in wait, / With lifted teeth, as if to bite! // Brave Admiral, say but one good word: / What shall we do when hope is gone?” / The words leapt like a leaping sword: / “Sail on! sail on! sail on! and on!”\nThen, pale and worn, he kept his deck, / And peered through darkness. Ah, that night / Of all dark nights! And then a speck— / A light! A light! A light! A light! // It grew, a starlit flag unfurled! / It grew to be Time’s burst of dawn. / He gained a world; he gave that world / Its grandest lesson: “On! sail on!”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c749e673-234e-4963-9cdf-0462ba50d71b",
                                                "sense_id": "bb2a8294-bcc9-37b1-9baf-92c84ed05fe2",
                                                "text": "The night continued beautifully clear and fine, and as we came into the fell country the outlines of the hills showed up dark against the starlit sky."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
